infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Per-slot Error vs throwing from batchLoadFn
  desc Same failure, opposite blast radius
  compares
    - label Return Error in a slot
      children
        - label Rejects only that one .load() Promise
        - label Other resolvers in the batch resolve normally
        - label Use for known failures: not found, no permission
        - label Apollo returns a partial response: one null field, one error
    - label Throw from batchLoadFn
      children
        - label Rejects ALL pending .load() Promises in the batch
        - label Every resolver in the request gets a rejection
        - label Even keys whose rows returned successfully fail
        - label Use only for catastrophic failure: database down
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
